{"step_index":155,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T00:23:06Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T09:23:06+09:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T09:23:09+09:00\nThe search for \"\"posys\" game OR \"posys\" indie OR \"posys\" steam OR \"posys\" \"김의준\"\" returned the following summary:\nThe term **\"posys\"** does not appear to refer to a specific indie game or a developer named Kim Eui-jun (김의준) in current search results. Instead, the term is likely a misspelling or a niche reference. Here is a breakdown of what the search results indicate:\n\n*   **\"Posy\" (YouTube/Cursor Creator):** There is a well-known creator named **Posy** who creates popular, aesthetic mouse cursor sets for Windows[1][2]. These are frequently distributed or utilized through the **\"Mouse X\"** app available on **Steam**[1][3][2]. This is the most common association with \"Posy\" and \"Steam.\"\n*   **\"POSYS\" (Business App):** There is an app called **POSYS M** (or \"포씨스M\") available on Google Play, which is a sales analysis tool for business owners to manage store performance, inventory, and sales data[4].\n*   **\"Pip and Posy\":** There is a popular children's book and media series titled *Pip and Posy*[5][6][7], but this is unrelated to indie gaming.\n*   **Misspellings in Gaming Contexts:** Online discussions (such as on Reddit or Steam) occasionally contain the typo \"posys\" in place of other words (often \"posts\" or \"posies\")[8][9][10], or in reference to specific in-game items or groups (e.g., characters in *Kingdom Come: Deliverance 2* are sometimes referred to as \"Posys\")[11].\n\nNo information was found linking \"posys\" to an indie game developer named Kim Eui-jun (김의준). It is possible that the name refers to a very small project or a different spelling is required.\n\nSources:\n[1] [centerpointgaming.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG4lxvv8cCybbMogv0SQNteyHElj8xKak2FMp5rot8FMTmL5zeiPEnGV3hNX5luLJw